# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the rawform UI app.
#
# This file is the no-rebuild STAGING area for triage: the proven floor is
# baked into the binary (ui/Sources/utils/SanitizerSuppressions.cpp), and
# anything here is ADDED on top of it for the run it is handed to. Deliver it
# from a terminal, not an IDE run configuration (CLion re-quotes values with
# '=' or ':' and the runtime then ignores them silently); options are
# comma-separated:
#
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=/path/to/rawform/ui/Sources/tools/tsan.supp \
#       ./rawform &> ~/tsan.txt
#
# ADMISSION CRITERIA, strict by design: a pattern lands here only when a
# report's BOTH racing stacks sit entirely in third-party frames (Qt, system
# libraries), so it cannot implicate rawform code. Provenance sections
# (allocation site, thread-creation site) naming rawform frames do NOT count
# as implication: they say who started the work, not who raced. Anything with
# a rawform frame in a racing stack must NOT be suppressed; it is ours to fix.
# Third-party is judged by AUTHORSHIP, not by which binary the frame lives in:
# code Qt's build tooling generates into the rawform executable (qmlcachegen's
# module loader) is Qt's, and a pattern anchored on the generated file name
# cannot reach a hand-written rawform frame.
#
# Context: the Qt frameworks in use are the prebuilt Online Installer
# binaries, which are NOT TSan-instrumented. The runtime therefore cannot see
# all synchronization Qt establishes internally, and some of Qt's own
# lifecycle choreography reports as racy regardless (partial-instrumentation
# blindness; the same mechanism class the sanitizer-profile note in
# audio/CMakeLists.txt describes).

# QtConcurrent ThreadEngine / IterateKernel self-deletion vs late pool-thread
# probes (shouldStartThread on a kernel being destroyed in
# asynchronousFinish). Observed at app exit on macOS/AppleClang with the
# MetadataReloader's revalidation map in flight; both racing stacks are
# QtConcurrent-internal. Any rawform-side QtConcurrent misuse would surface
# with rawform frames in a racing stack and would NOT match this pattern
# alone; keep it scoped to the QtConcurrent namespace.
race:QtConcurrent::

# qmlcachegen's generated module loader (rawform_qmlcache_loader.cpp): the
# Q_GLOBAL_STATIC Registry QHash of compiled QML units, freed by the atexit
# handler on the main thread, against a read of the same hash by the QML type
# loader thread (QQmlMetaType::findCachedCompilationUnit, on a QThread the
# QML engine started). Reported three times per exit, one per heap field the
# destructor frees. The thread is joined in ~QQmlEngine, long before main()
# returns; the join is QThread::wait, a futex-based QMutex/QWaitCondition on
# Linux, invisible to the runtime with the uninstrumented Qt binaries, so the
# real happens-before never reaches TSan. Both racing stacks are the
# generated TU plus libQt6Qml; called_from_lib does not cover it because the
# accesses are issued from the (instrumented) generated code, not from inside
# the library. Linux/GCC only; the macOS runtime sees the join. Baked into
# SanitizerSuppressions.cpp once the macOS run confirmed it absent there.
race:rawform_qmlcache_loader.cpp
